# Root-level .dockerignore for `metap-org` itself (first one — every other .dockerignore in this
# flat multi-repo directory belongs to 1 repo and only applies when that repo is its own build
# context). Needed because `metap-demo-waf/data-plane/web/Dockerfile` is the first build in this
# whole org whose context has to be the metap-org ROOT, not 1 repo — it needs `design-system/` and
# `platform-ui/` visible alongside `metap-demo-waf/` to resolve their `link:../design-system`/
# `link:../../../design-system` pnpm dependencies (see that Dockerfile's own top comment). Without
# this file, that build's context would include every sibling repo's `target/`/`node_modules/`
# wholesale — verified live (2026-09-01) at ~49GB combined across just the 4 Rust repos' `target/`
# alone, before counting `node_modules/`. Only read for a build whose context is this directory;
# does not affect `metap/docker-compose.yml`, `metap-demo-crm/Dockerfile`, etc., which all build
# from their own repo as context and read that repo's own `.dockerignore` instead.
**/target
/.shared-target
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.env
**/dist
**/.DS_Store
**/keys/*.pem
